Question - Given an array of strings strs, group all anagrams together into sublists. You may return the output in any order.

An anagram is a string that contains the exact same characters as another string, but the order of the characters can be different.

Link - https://neetcode.io/problems/anagram-groups/question?list=neetcode150

Coding 
---------*-------------------*-------------------------------*---------------------------*---------------
class Solution {
    public List<List<String>> groupAnagrams(String[] strs) {
Map<String,List<String>> m = new HashMap<>();
for(String str : strs)
{
    char[] cr = str.toCharArray(); //convert string to character array 
    Arrays.sort(cr);
    String sort = new String(cr); // convert character array back to string 

m.putIfAbsent(sort,new ArrayList<>());
m.get(sort).add(str);
}      
return new ArrayList<>(m.values());
    }
}
